Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::overlap_is_exactly_sharing_a_block`.

The defect: `Entry::overlaps` compares with `<` where `last_lba` is inclusive. Two partitions that meet in one
block (one ends exactly where the next begins) are reported as disjoint.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(a.overlaps(&b), shared)`.

diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
index 04d4270c8..1344cf887 100644
--- a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
+++ b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
@@ -194,3 +194,3 @@ impl Entry {
             && other.is_used()
-            && self.first_lba <= other.last_lba
+            && self.first_lba < other.last_lba
             && other.first_lba <= self.last_lba
